commit 8f42cb7d87175e996d2b81473200e5920d6a3ba3
Author: 仓鼠王 <yjianbin419@gmail.com>
Date:   Wed Sep 23 03:53:40 2026 +0800

    feat(frontend): the hub names the stop a hard rule dropped, in words and not in ids (ORD-0232)
    
    A candidate the feasibility gate drops leaves an audit event whose only place-naming field is
    "<RULE>_ACCESS_UNAVAILABLE:<place_id>", and nothing on the traveller's screen accounted for the
    missing stop.  The hub now reads that feed, resolves the id through the places directory it already
    has, and says which stop went and which condition it failed.  An id the directory cannot resolve is
    reported as unreadable rather than printed raw, and an unknown rule code falls back to "unnamed
    condition" instead of a prettified enum.
    
    Each node owns one claim with a mutant of its own, so no single killer covers two contracts; the
    painted-versus-spoken judgement lives only in the node that asserts it.

